      "en": "RAYMOND (Scene 14, turn 133): This is not a whim, Marcelle; it is the demand of ontological truth. We built our comfort upon a dispossession shrouded in silence. We experience thus the liberating power of the fresh gaze that dissolves false pretenses and re-establishes the demand of ontological authenticity."
